      "sampler": "Occil.PSRN.newSimplex",
      "public_spec": "SampLib.PSRNSimplex.newSimplex_vectorSpec",
      "spec_kind": "latent_vector",
      "classification": "core",
      "reviewed_domain": "Every dimension n>=1; n<=0 fails in the actual source guard. Target law: uniform on the open standard simplex, i.e. m! times Lebesgue measure on {y>0, sum y<1} in R^m embedded by appending 1-sum y (n=m+1), proved for the spec's own world/output/initial (output_law_uniform). The result is the actual list of n jointly owned deferred coordinate oracles over one unit-rate exponential world (n=1: constant 1/1, world unobserved; n>=2: actual exponentials normalized by one shared sum), with arbitrary joint ENNReal credits including infinity, all natural read precisions and repeated aliases. Only UniformInt randomness is needed.",
